COMMENT Written for WoW Model Viewer's light catalogue (wow::LightCatalog: the zone light's water colours,
COMMENT docs/world-viewer/09-liquids.md). The layouts come from public table definitions, read as hypotheses: the four
COMMENT alphas the catalogue reads (database.xml, table LightParams) were checked against the clients' own bytes; the other
COMMENT columns are named by their field index, their types and widths the hypotheses' (never read). A neutral name that
COMMENT two layouts share is the same slot in the column order (after Classic's inline ID), not an established equal
COMMENT meaning. Fields 0-31 are the same columns in CAE394E7 and A7F31923 (the four alphas agree on all 3745 rows Retail and
COMMENT PTR share). Every field is listed in file order. Most Retail rows are copy rows: LightData and Light refer to copy
COMMENT IDs directly. A layout not listed here is not read.

